 had been handed. The engine preferred B6, which White took on the next move."}, {"turn": 36, "text": "Opus 5.5's A3 lost 16.9 points and moved Black's lead from -5.7 to +11.2. The engine wanted B9, and it kept naming B9 for White through the next several turns. This was the first of ten moves in a row that each lost 14.0 points or more."}, {"turn": 44, "text": "H1 was Opus 5.5's worst move, losing 24.1 points and turning Black's lead from -5.9 to +18.2. The engine's choice was B8, the same corner point it had pointed to for several turns."}, {"turn": 45, "text": "The 12k answered with J4, which lost 27.0 points, the biggest loss of the game, and sent the lead from +18.2 to -8.8. The engine's choice was B8."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "after.py places one move the player names, removes captures, and prints group liberties; libs.py prints liberties for the current board; count.py counts stones and enclosed territory. None of them loops over candidate moves, scores moves, or plays out continuations, so they only inspect the current position and the effect of a single named move.", "stop": false}}